==============================================================================
STEP 2 — constraint rank and solution-set parameterization
F1 = 4*a0^2 - G*c^2*rho_L = 0   (this is a0 = (c/2)*sqrt(G*rho_L), squared; encodes kappa = 1/2)
F2 = Lambda - 8*pi*G*rho_L/c^2 = 0
Jacobian J(F1,F2)/d(a0, rho_L, Lambda) =
Matrix([[8*a0, -G*c**2, 0], [0, -8*pi*G/c**2, 1]])
rank(J) = 2  (rows independent for a0 > 0: row1 has dF1/da0 = 8*a0 != 0, row2 has dF2/dLambda = 1)
rank < number of variables (3)  =>  solution set is a 1-parameter family:
  (rho_L, a0, Lambda) = (lambda, (c/2)*sqrt(G*lambda), 8*pi*G*lambda/c^2),  lambda > 0

CONTROL 1 — rearranged copies of F1 treated as new equations
Jacobian of the 5-copy system w.r.t. (a0, rho_L), evaluated OFF the curve (generic point):
rank (generic) = 2   [copies are not idempotent as functions; the test is the solution set]
After substituting the on-curve relations (4a0^2 = G c^2 rho, sqrt(G rho) = 2 a0/c):
rank (on the solution curve) = 1

Full copy system {F1a..F1e, F2, F2b} w.r.t. (a0, rho, Lambda), on the curve:
rank = 2  (still 2: 7 written equations, 2 constraint directions, 1-dim family — no new constraint created by rewriting)

